
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Appended to the generated version file by alt's own CMakeLists.txt.
#
# EXPLANATORY ONLY. The comparison above -- generated by
# write_basic_package_version_file with COMPATIBILITY SameMinorVersion --
# remains the sole authority on what is accepted. This block never sets
# PACKAGE_VERSION_COMPATIBLE or PACKAGE_VERSION_EXACT; it only explains a
# refusal that has already been decided, because CMake's own report of one
# says just "the version found is not compatible with the version requested"
# and names neither the rule nor a remedy.
#
# @PROJECT_VERSION@ is substituted at configure time rather than read from
# PACKAGE_VERSION, which the bitness check above may already have rewritten
# to "@PROJECT_VERSION@ (32bit)".
#
# The PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION guard is load-bearing: on a versionless
# find_package(Alt) the generated comparison leaves PACKAGE_VERSION_COMPATIBLE
# FALSE -- it compares an empty requested major against this one -- and CMake
# then ignores it, accepting the package. Without the guard this block would
# announce a refusal that is not happening, to a caller who requested no
# version at all.
#
# The remedy is deliberately one sentence and not a branch on the direction of
# the mismatch. "Install @PROJECT_VERSION@ or newer" reads as the obvious
# advice for a request above the installed version and is false under
# SameMinorVersion, which rejects a later MINOR just as firmly as an earlier
# one: only the requested minor series, at or above the requested patch, can
# satisfy the request.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
if(PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION AND NOT PACKAGE_VERSION_COMPATIBLE AND NOT ${PACKAGE_FIND_NAME}_FIND_QUIETLY)
  message(STATUS
    "alt @PROJECT_VERSION@ is installed here, but ${PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION} was requested.\n"
    "   alt accepts only a request for the same minor release (@PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR@.@PROJECT_VERSION_MINOR@.x).\n"
    "   The inline sizes of its async primitives (async_event, async_mutex, task_group, ...)\n"
    "   can change between minor releases: those types are embedded by value in the headers,\n"
    "   while their out-of-line definitions ship in libalt, so headers and library from\n"
    "   different minor releases are a layout mismatch with no other diagnostic.\n"
    "   Install alt ${PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION_MAJOR}.${PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION_MINOR}.x at "
    "${PACKAGE_FIND_VERSION} or later, or ask for find_package(Alt @PROJECT_VERSION@).")
endif()
